# Verify browser exceptions via curl (required)

When the developer provides a **URL** and reports a **clear exception visible in the browser** (stack trace, error banner, 5xx error page, Next.js/Vite overlay text), do not claim a fix is working until it is verified.

## Rule (guardrail)

- Do not claim a fix works until it is verified with a bounded curl of the reported URL(s).
- Prefer curling from the same network context the app uses (compose service / app container when host curl cannot reach the URL).
- Pair with `umbraculum-toolset-common` rule `45-public-endpoint-verification` for the wrap-up `Endpoint verification: ...` summary line on non-doc service changes.

## Runbook

See `curl-exception-verification` skill.
